    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλύρ-ῐνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of lime wood,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σανίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ostr.Bodl.</u>
				iii 267
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				67.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> (Leonid.Sch.) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.20.74
			</span></i>; <i>light as lime wood,</i> of Cinesias, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1377
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.adloc.; but <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				12.551d
			</span></i> thinks it means that <i>he wore stays of lime
		wood.</i></div>
